  "details": "a common issue with earmuffs is not knowing if somebody's trying to talk to you. I'd like to be able to apply a lowpass filter to voices in the falloff range of earmuffs mode. it would allow me to hear if someone is talking without the sibilants and word interpretation sapping signal processing power from my brain. I could then choose to get closer to them to hear what they're saying.\n\nThis would be an additional slider in the UI for lowpass frequency. voices within the inner radius would have a cutoff of 20,000 hz (or whatever the world sets the already-existing lowpass to) and voices outside the outer radius would have a cutoff of this value (or the world value, whichever is lower)\n\nAlso, if OSC is implemented for earmuff settings, tools like OyasumiVR would be able to automatically muffle everyone while sleeping (but still have them audible, just unintelligible)",
